# stage-a-pilot1-harness-gemma.plan — same real task as
# stage-a-pilot1-harness.plan, but explicitly on gemma3:1b instead of
# letting CHOOSE_MODEL route to stable-code:latest, to test whether
# the earlier §10 finding (smaller model = less pollution) holds for
# a harness-writing task too, not just single-line code generation.
SET_MODEL | gemma3:1b | true
STEP | give me a bash test script for a program. the script should make a temporary items.txt file containing item_5=10, start the prisc+x virtual machine binary (path passed as argument 1) on a .pal file (path passed as argument 2), then check items.txt afterward equals item_5=13, and print PASS or FAIL. reply with only the bash script, no explanation, no markdown fences | grep -qi "pass\|fail" "$STEP2_OUT"
STEP | write /tmp/claude-1000/scratchpad/stage_a_pilot/test_harness_gemma.sh | true | APPROVE
